<title>MEXICO: Mexico stocks roar to record close.</title>
<headline>Mexico stocks roar to record close.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican stocks rallied to a record close on Tuesday on heavy demand for stocks from foreign traders and expectations that primary rates were about to fall to their lowest level since the December 1994 peso devaluation crisis.</p>
<p>Preliminary closing figures for the leading IPC share index were up 70.90 points, or 1.93 percent, at 3,750.03.</p>
<p>((-- Martin Roberts, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7907)).</p>
